Responsibilities
GENERAL FUNCTIONS:
Under the direct supervision of the Media Analyst, the incumbent will assist with the following tasks
Assist in acquiring knowledge of the media laws and regulations;
Assist in assessing the state and private media;
Provide the Media Analyst with the relevant information on the media situation in connection with the elections;
Assist in collecting all press reporting on the Election Observation Mission;
Monitor a sample of local Media (TV, radio, and newspaper) using quantitative and qualitative methodology provided by the Media Expert to measure time, Plan and Tone devoted to political parties and candidates and produce daily monitoring reports for the Media Expert.
Assist the Media Analyst during meetings with representatives of the Media.
Assist in the preparation of a short briefing for the Observers and a short assessment for the Chief Observer in preparation for the Press Release and Preliminary Statement;
Assist in the preparation of a written report on the media for the Final Report;
Assisting the Media Analyst in the preparation of press kits for eventual press conferences conducted by the mission.
Any other tasks as may be required.
Education:
Possesses a university degree in journalism or communication or marketing, and/or adequate training and relevant work experience, which may be accepted in lieu of a university degree.
go to method of application »

Responsibilities
GENERAL FUNCTIONS: Under the direct supervision of the Social Media Analyst, the incumbent will assist with the following tasks:
Monitor the online platforms of a sample list of political and electoral contestants, key state institutions officials, relevant opinion leaders, third-party campaign accounts, others;
Track the strategies used by candidates and parties to campaign on the main online platforms and the extent of campaign advertisement;
Identify the presence of hate/inciteful speech, incitement to violence against certain groups of voters, candidates and party supporters;
Identify disinformation efforts during the campaign as well as possible interference in the integrity of the electoral process via bots, trolls and other forms of orchestrated campaigns;
Analysis should also focus on how women candidates and marginalized groups are portrayed in social media, digital literacy efforts, and allegations of intimidation and online violence;
Assist in acquiring knowledge of the general media landscape and existent regulatory framework for online content;
Create social media monitoring data bases and prepare qualitative and quantitative reports on the assigned online platforms;
